      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Yuval,\nThe build error is because the Kohaku board is still using Zephyr v2.5. There are two approaches to fix it:\n1. cherry-pick the upstream change like CL:3054142 also to v2.5.\n2. change Kohaku to use Zephyr v2.6.\nPlease advise which one you prefer.",
      "parentUuid": "edf654ba_22c68d9c",
      "revId": "1275d4ff577a354ea5a1a1b9f301045fe7ae5f05",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "10b57100_cf7aac66",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/chip/npcx/espi.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1333748
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-04T03:16:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh wow, this is what I was worried about with our versions.\n\nI think that #1 is too complicated, I\u0027m worried there are other dependencies that will be hard to find and I really don\u0027t want to establish this as a pattern (otherwise why even have versions).\n\n#2 is possible and is likely the easiest, but I also don\u0027t like it as a pattern, we shouldn\u0027t need to update ALL the boards every time we uprev, otherwise again, why even have versions?\n\nThere\u0027s a 3rd option, I added a macro a while back `IS_ZEPHYR_VERSION(major, minor)` to be able to run code differently on different versions of Zephyr.\n\nHow hard would it be to use that here?",
      "parentUuid": "ae199bd3_d00c56f4",
      "revId": "1275d4ff577a354ea5a1a1b9f301045fe7ae5f05",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
